732|n|of Bass ; An edible, spiny-finned fish, esp. of the genera Roccus, Labrax, and related genera. There are many species. ; The two American fresh-water species of black bass (genus Micropterus). See Black bass. ; Species of Serranus, the sea bass and rock bass. See Sea bass. ; The southern, red, or channel bass (Sciaena ocellata). See Redfish. ; The linden or lime tree, sometimes wrongly called whitewood; also, its bark, which is used for making mats. See Bast. ; A hassock or thick mat.	N:9do,130,2~9do,130,2
